course: dictionary
lesson: 4711
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Hood is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which are its context. «The king cobra spreads its neck ribs into a hood as a warning» tells you a hood can be a shape on an animal, not a piece of clothing.
explain: Names can also contain ordinary words. «Historians do not know whether Robin Hood was one real person» is not about a coat. Robin is a person's name, so Hood is part of a name here. Always ask: what does the sentence say this word is?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «Put your hood up, it is pouring with rain» works with a coat hood, because you can pull a coat hood up when it rains. Swapping in the meaning is the best check.
fact: A hood is a part of a coat or jumper that you can pull up to cover your head.
fact: A hood can also be a cover over something, like a cooker hood that takes away smoke.
fact: In US English, the hood is the metal cover over a car's engine. In UK English, that is called the bonnet.
fact: Informal US slang uses hood to mean a neighbourhood, so «my hood» means «my area».
fact: Hoods can block your side vision, so look carefully both ways before you cross the road.
exercise: «A cobra spreads its hood, a rattlesnake buzzes its rattle and a black mamba opens its inky black mouth.» What is the hood here? | *The flat skin a cobra spreads around its neck as a warning | A waterproof jacket for the snake | A cover for the cooker | The bonnet of a car
exercise: «Historians do not know whether Robin Hood was one real person.» What is Hood part of in this sentence? | A cover that takes away smoke | The metal cover over an engine | *A person's name | A coat you pull up when it rains
exercise: «Put your hood up, it is pouring with rain.» What does hood mean? | *Part of a coat you pull up over your head | A cover over the engine of a car | A cooker cover that takes away smoke | A neighbourhood
test: An American says, «Look under the hood before we drive.» What does hood mean? | A jumper with a zip | The skin around a snake's neck | *The metal cover over the car's engine | A cover for a cooker
test: «Wild wolves are shy, and old stories like Little Red Riding Hood come from times when people feared wolves.» What clue shows that Hood is part of a story name? | Feared means scared of a coat | *Little Red Riding is a girl's name in a story, so Hood is part of it | Wolves are shy, so hood means a shy animal | Times means a clock
exam: Jayden reads, «Stay out of my hood, it's not safe at night.» What does hood mean in this informal US slang? | A cooker cover | A coat that covers your head | A car's bonnet | *A neighbourhood, the area where someone lives
